        `IGAE arrives first, covers one month and can be revised. GDP arrives later and covers the full quarter. I would want several stronger IGAE readings and confirmation in the next GDP release before calling a recovery.`],
       chart:{title:'Economic activity, annual percent change by month',stat:`${signed(G.value,1,'%')}`,series:[line('IGAE annual change',igae.slice(-72),GREEN,v=>fmt(v,1)+'%')],yFormat:v=>fmt(v,1)+'%',label:'IGAE annual percentage change by month',srcId:'banxico-igae'}},
      {h2:`Investment rebounded in April; foreign investment hit a record`,
       prose:[`${investmentFact?esc(investmentFact.fact):'Fixed investment has weakened as a share of the economy.'}`,
        `${fdiFact?esc(fdiFact.fact):'Foreign-investment headlines include both new projects and money reinvested by companies already operating in Mexico.'}`,
        `${creditFact?esc(creditFact.fact):''} That ratio includes total financing. The monthly series on this site is narrower: the nominal stock of commercial-bank credit to the private nonfinancial sector was ${CY?fmt(pct(C.value,CY.value),1)+'% above a year earlier':'still growing'} in ${dateLabel(C.date)}. That is growth from a shallow base. I want to see whether the financing becomes machinery, construction, formal hiring and higher output.`]},
